<InfoPanel Title="How this connects to the evidence workflow"
           Subtitle="The role model protects the same Week 3 workflow rather than changing the app shape."
           Tone="success">

    <div class="of-link-row">
        <span class="of-badge of-badge-info">Authenticated user</span>
        <span>→</span>
        <span class="of-badge of-badge-success">Role mapping</span>
        <span>→</span>
        <span class="of-badge of-badge-warning">Policy check</span>
        <span>→</span>
        <span class="of-badge of-badge-info">Record action</span>
        <span>→</span>
        <span class="of-badge of-badge-muted">Activity Log</span>
    </div>

    <p class="of-muted-text">
        In Week 4, upload, delete, export, settings, and role-management actions should be protected by policy.
        The app should keep the Week 3 workflow shape: record details → upload evidence → Document Library → Data Quality/Reports → Activity Log.
    </p>
</InfoPanel>

<GuidanceNote Title="Block 9 outcome" Icon="✅" Tone="info">
    <p>
        User Roles now defines the production-ready role and permission model for OperationsFlow.
        Week 4 should connect this model to Microsoft Entra ID and enforce the policies in real application code.
    </p>
</GuidanceNote>